course: dictionary
lesson: 12687
title: Paths that split apart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When two things start in the same place and then go different ways, we say they diverge. Think of a road with a fork in it: at the fork, the one road becomes two. «At the fork, the two paths diverge: one goes to the lake and the other climbs the hill.»
explain: Diverge is a verb, so it changes its ending: diverges, diverged, diverging. Use it when things move apart. «The river and the railway diverged near the old mill, so we lost sight of the train.»
explain: Diverge can also be about ideas. When opinions or plans diverge, they stop matching. «At first we agreed on the game, but our views on the rules soon diverged.» Check the meaning by swapping in «separated» or «went different ways»: if it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Diverge means to go in different directions from the same point.
fact: «Diverge» is a verb: diverge, diverges, diverged, diverging.
fact: Light rays diverge when they spread out from one point, like the light from a torch.
fact: In maths, a series diverges when it does not settle on one number.
fact: Use «diverge from» to show what something splits away from, as in «the path diverged from the main road».
exercise: «The two paths diverge at the big oak tree.» What does diverge mean here? | Come together into one path | *Go off in different directions | Disappear into the ground | Stop and wait for everyone
exercise: Sam and Priya agreed at first, but now their views diverge. What does that mean? | They have finished the project | They are both asleep | They have joined together | *Their opinions have become different
exercise: «The light rays diverge from the lamp.» What is the rays doing? | Growing dimmer and dimmer | Going out and never coming back | Shining into one small spot | *Spreading out in different directions from one point
test: «The river and the road diverge near the bridge.» What does diverge mean? | Freeze in place | Run side by side forever | Meet and join up | *Split apart and go different ways
test: A maths series diverges when it does not do what? | Use whole numbers | Get bigger each time | *Settle on one number | Contain any numbers at all
exam: «Our plans diverged after the school trip, so we went different ways.» What does diverged mean? | Became the same as each other | Were written down carefully | *Became different from each other | Were cancelled completely
